{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BufferingResource"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Expensive interaction with the underlying resource is minimized, since most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(smaller) requests can be satisfied by accessing the buffer alone. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"drawback is that some extra space is required to hold the buffer and that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copying takes place when filling that buffer, but this is usually","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outweighed by the performance benefits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that this implementation is pretty limited and the benefits are only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apparent when reading forward and consecutively – e.g. when downloading the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resource by chunks. The buffer is ignored when reading backward or far","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ahead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/Loggable","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/Resource","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/Streamable","doc:\/\/Readium\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Readium\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Readium\/ScA"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/bufferingresource"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","t